    "cell": "B1",
    "formula_or_input": "May 2025 Rating effect: On May 16, 2025, Moody's, the lone holdout among the ratings agencies, downgraded the United States from Aaa to Aa1, thus raising questions about whether the US 10-year treasury rate is really a riskfree rate. Netting out the default spread for an Aa1 rated sovereign from the US treasury rate will yield a more consistent riskfree rate in US dollars and a higher equity risk premium. While I will report my conventional measure of the ERP, with the US treasury rate as the riskfree rate, to allow for comparison with time series data, I will also report a US ERP with the adjusted riskfree rate.",
